number|title|condition|evidence|remediation|limitation|attack|nist|nist_rationale|sources|severity
001|Remote Desktop provides unintended access to a hybrid bridge|A lower-trust principal has effective RDP logon authorization to a bridge host AND approved network evidence shows an allowed route from its zone.|Allow and deny logon rights; group expansion; firewall/network policy; host role; account restrictions.|Restrict remote logon identities and source zones and use the protected administrative path.|RDP listening does not establish reachability or authorization. NLA is not a replacement for least-privilege access.|T1021.001|AC-3;AC-17;SC-7|Constrain remote administrative access to the hybrid control plane.||High
002|WinRM exposes privileged execution on a hybrid bridge|A lower-trust principal can reach a WinRM endpoint AND its effective endpoint configuration permits privileged execution on a bridge host.|Endpoint security descriptor; JEA/session configuration; run-as identity; network rules; host role.|Restrict endpoint authorization and run-as privilege and use narrowly scoped administration.|WinRM enabled is not arbitrary command execution. JEA command limits and deny rules may materially constrain the route.|T1021.006|AC-3;AC-17;CM-7|Restrict remote management capability and privileged execution scope.||High
003|An SMB relay candidate reaches a bridge with useful authorization|A bridge accepts relayable NTLM over an SMB path without required signing AND a supported reachable authentication source would have useful target rights.|Server/client signing policy; NTLM restrictions; approved reachability evidence; source account rights; bridge classification.|Require supported SMB protection and reduce NTLM and unnecessary administrative paths.|Unsigned SMB alone is not a working relay. No coercion or relay is performed by this project.|T1557.001;T1021.002|SC-8;AC-3;CM-6|Protect authenticated file and administrative communication to identity infrastructure.|MS-SMB|High
004|An LDAP relay candidate can change objects feeding the tenant|A DC exposes a supported relayable LDAP authentication path AND the relayed identity could modify a source object whose supported sync flow affects sensitive cloud authorization.|Effective LDAP signing/CBT; authentication mode; source/reachability evidence; precise object write; synchronization mapping.|Enforce supported LDAP protections and restrict the downstream object-write authority.|LDAP signing and TLS channel binding solve different conditions. A single registry value is not the complete effective state.|T1557;T1098|SC-8;AC-3;CM-6|Protect directory authentication and the integrity of authorization inputs.|MS-LDAP|High
005|LAPS retrieval authorization reaches a hybrid bridge outside its tier|An unapproved principal can retrieve or decrypt the managed local administrator credential for a hybrid bridge AND that local identity has effective administrative access.|LAPS storage mode; managed account; retrieval/decryption ACL or role; effective host authorization; approved tier.|Restrict LAPS retrieval and decryption authorization to the protected administrative boundary.|Never retrieve the password. Entra-backed and AD-backed LAPS require different authorization evaluation.|T1078.003|AC-3;AC-6;IA-5|Protect managed local authenticators according to the host's identity-control role.|MS-LAPS|High
006|Virtualization administration reaches a hybrid control-plane machine|A lower-trust principal has effective hypervisor or VM-management capability sufficient to control a guest that runs a hybrid bridge or domain controller.|VM-to-host binding; scoped virtualization role; console/disk/guest-execution capabilities; guest role and tenant linkage.|Protect virtualization management at the same boundary as the identity guests it can control.|Read-only inventory access is not guest control. Encryption and independent key custody can constrain disk-only access.|T1078;T1003|AC-6;SC-7;CM-5|Align management-plane access with the sensitive guest systems it governs.||High
007|Backup restoration rights permit replacement of a hybrid bridge|An unapproved principal can restore or replace a bridge's machine state through the backup platform with sufficient execution or credential-use impact.|Backup role and scope; supported restore destination; approval boundary; guest binding; bridge responsibility.|Separate backup recovery authorization for control-plane assets and require independent approval.|Backup read and restore authority differ. A restore requiring an independent approver is not unilateral host control.|T1078;T1556.007|AC-5;AC-6;CP-10|Control recovery operations capable of changing identity infrastructure.||High
008|Endpoint management can deploy code to a hybrid bridge from a lower tier|A lower-trust management operator can deploy software, scripts, or policies that execute with high privilege on a bridge host.|Management-platform role; device collection membership; deployment scope; run-as semantics; independent approval; host role.|Separate control-plane device collections and restrict deployment authority.|A listed device is not proof of deployment authority. Read-only roles and enforced approval gates may block execution.|T1072;T1556.007|AC-6;CM-3;CM-5|Restrict centralized deployment authority over hybrid identity infrastructure.||High
